    39	The guide prompt states both artifact shapes literally, with one filled example each (#260). A
    40	guide that has not read `prewalk.py` still has everything it needs, because a semantically correct
    41	artifact in another dialect fails the transition and terminalizes the run *after* the guide turn
    42	has already been paid for. Two bounds are normalized rather than enforced: a `summary` longer than
    43	500 characters is truncated, and an absent or null `validation_attempted` becomes an empty list.
    44	Everything else stays fail-closed. Leniency never fabricates evidence — a prose `validation`
    45	string is not coerced into a `{command, exit_code}` record, because that would invent an exit code
    46	the guide never observed — and it never touches identity, schema version, `PW-##` ordering, or the
    47	literal `ready_for_execution_model: true` assertion.
    48
    49	Live qualification records the route it **observed**, not the route it requested (#258). The
    50	canary derives `route_change` from provider evidence: when a host names the model it actually
    51	resumed with, that name must match the requested execution model or qualification fails with
    52	`prewalk_route_change_unqualified`. Codex publishes such a notice (an `item.completed` whose inner
    53	item type is `error`, naming both the recorded and the resuming model) and publishes it only when
    54	the model actually changes; Claude Code, Grok Build, and Oh My Pi publish nothing comparable
    55	today. Absence of a signal is not evidence that an override was ignored, so it never fails closed
    56	— the artifact records `route_change_evidence: unobserved` and an empty `observed_execution_route`
    57	instead of claiming behavioural proof. No host publishes the reasoning level it actually used, so
    58	observed effort is always null rather than copied from the request.
    59
    60	The model-free transition validator requires a clean registered start, unchanged branch/origin/
    61	protected refs, a real source/test/product-documentation edit tied to the checkpoint, no forbidden
    62	surface, and no `Close` commit. Runtime-only, plan-only, execution-log-only, empty, mismatched, or
    63	out-of-worktree changes fail closed. A tiny atomic task may finish after the guide only when every
    64	TODO item is complete and the checkpoint explicitly says `task_complete`; a zero guide exit alone
    65	never means completion.
    66
    67	The version-3 private native-worker state records requested and actual mode, both phase routes,
    68	capability and instruction-fidelity evidence, packet digest/count, status history, attempts,
    69	session/worktree continuity, transition proof, bounded diagnostics, and fallback. Version-2
